#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055538} :activity/id #uuid "633bd081-e2bc-5558-98c8-fc2d194682a2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048511 :topic/id #uuid "a58ee80d-63c3-55fb-ab64-be5e78c6d9c5" :topic/math-academy-id 31} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055967 :tutorial/content "To add complex numbers, we just add the real parts and add the imaginary parts separately. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5\\text{i})+(2-3\\text{i}) & =(3+5\\text{i})+(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+2)+(5+(-\\,3))\\text{i} \\\\  & =(3+2)+(5-3)\\text{i} \\\\  & =5+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, we write\n\n$$\n(a + b\\textrm{i}) + (c + d\\textrm{i}) = (a + c) + (b + d)\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\nSubtracting complex numbers works in the same way: we just subtract the real parts and subtract the imaginary parts separately. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5\\text{i})-(2-3\\text{i}) & =(3+5\\text{i})-(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3-2)+(5-(-\\,3))\\text{i} \\\\  & =(3-2)+(5+3)\\text{i} \\\\  & =1+8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, we write\n\n$$\n(a + b\\textrm{i}) - (c + d\\textrm{i}) = (a - c) + (b - d)\\textrm{i}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3783edad-ba1d-564c-8e99-3ba74795716f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2788 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4ec81b99-be36-51f9-b8c9-9de86abfdb21" :step/math-academy-id 14292 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055539}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055539 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054618 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054529 :question/id #uuid "f6b5bac8-9d99-50d8-91a9-c4d74cc67845" :question/math-academy-id "e-4036"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f13e54-35a5-5eca-a35a-292e26c6c2da" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049565} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050452}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054974} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055426} {:db/id #e